Basic concept:
	A retro OS for late 80s PC hardware - target hardware is the amstrac PC1512 with 512KB RAM and two floppies
	Multitasking with 4 virtual consoles + potentially one serial console

Task slots:
	There are 5 slots (for now)
	Slot 0 is the kernel itself, loaded into segment 1000h by the bootloader
	Slots 1-4 are user tasks

Virtual consoles:
	4 virtual consoles activated using ctrl-alt-F1 through to ctrl-alt-F4

Task templates:
	A task template is a compressed memory dump and register state loaded from disk
	A task template can be loaded into any of the 1-4 user task slots - representing the 4 user consoles
	When the user hits ctrl-alt-S, the kernel suspends whatever task is on that virtual console and displays a menu:
		Save task
			Serializes the task to disk as a new template
		Save data
			Serializes only parts of memory the user program marked as dynamic state (for example, the edit buffer of a text editor)
		Load task
			Loads a new task from disk, replacing this one
		Save all tasks
			Saves all tasks to disk
		Load tasks
			Loads multiple tasks from a task container (a file containing >1 tasks serialized to disk)
		Terminate task
			Terminates the task - just stops the task, resets to the default task (shell)

The shell
	Default user task1

Boot floppy
	A boot floppy is just a floppy containing a kernel image and filesystem metadata saying it's bootable
	Once the kernel is resident, the boot floppy can be removed

Filesystem
	The filesystem represents files as chains of blocks - a block is 512 bytes (1 sector), the name can be 25 characters long (this might be changed)
	For defrag:
		Defrag tool asks the user to terminate sufficient tasks to free up enough memory (usually this just means closing all tasks, avoiding potential filesystem access too)
		Entire disk is read into memory and written back out, with a warning not to shutdown - user can optionally insert a different floppy if desired
	Task templates take a maximum of 128 blocks (plus metadata stored in reserved filesystem blocks)
	This allows 5 entire tasks, plus 80 reserved blocks - though reserved blocks may change
